From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Alejandro G. Castro" <alex@igalia.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:16:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] [WPE][Android] Send trace points, signposts and counters
 to ATrace https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328971

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

Add an ATrace backend for Android analysis. Perfetto keeps only
the first of repeated begins with the same key, so a load that begins
again on a redirect is still timed from its first begin.
ScrollingThreadRenderUpdateSync begins on the main thread and ends on
the scrolling thread, so it is a process-scoped section too.

Signposts are keyed by a pointer and may begin and end on different threads,
so they map to process-scoped sections with a cookie derived from that
pointer. Perfetto pairs those by name, so a signpost's description goes out
as a separate zero-length marker instead of being folded into the name.
ATrace cannot backdate an event, so the signposts that carry their own
timestamp or time delta are dropped.

The backend is selected by a new USE_ATRACE_CAPTURE build option. It is
only offered when building for Android, where it is on by default, and
it conflicts with USE_SYSPROF_CAPTURE, which now defaults to off there
since Android has no Sysprof.

ATrace_beginAsyncSection() and ATrace_setCounter() need API level 29.

